<Project>

  <!--
    Everything the build generates goes under artifacts/ at the repository root, outside every
    project folder, so no project's default globs can read it back as source. .NET projects put
    bin and obj there through UseArtifactsOutput; Engine.vcxproj puts its output there through
    ArtifactsPath. The engine's dependencies live in 3rdParty/ instead, so that cleaning
    artifacts/ never forces them to be downloaded and compiled again.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version Condition="'$(Version)' == ''">1.0.0</Version>
    <ArtifactsPath>$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)artifacts</ArtifactsPath>
    <UseArtifactsOutput>true</UseArtifactsOutput>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Generated folders that still appear inside a project folder are never build input.

    WHY THIS EXISTS. The WinUI XAML compiler writes a copy of each XAML file into a "bin-fl"
    folder, resolving "$(BaseOutputPath)-fl" against the wrong working directory. That copy lands
    INSIDE the output tree. The SDK's default globs then pick it up as SOURCE on the next build,
    the compiler writes another copy one level deeper, and the path grows without bound on every
    build. It reached 18 directory levels here and broke the build with
    "Xaml Internal Error WMC9999: Could not find a part of the path".

    The compiler is a binary we cannot patch. But the recursion only compounds because build
    output re-enters the build as input. Test runs leave TestResults folders inside test projects
    the same way. Excluding these folders, at any depth, from the default item globs breaks that
    loop, so the folders can be written but never consumed, and depth stays constant.

    This must be the DefaultItemExcludes property, not item Remove lines. MSBuild reads every
    property before any item, so the exclusion is in place when the SDK and Windows App SDK
    globs run; a Remove here runs before those globs exist and removes nothing.

    Do not remove these without re-testing that a repeated build does not create or deepen a
    bin-fl folder.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <DefaultItemExcludes>$(DefaultItemExcludes);**/bin/**;**/obj/**;**/bin-fl/**;**/TestResults/**</DefaultItemExcludes>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
